# tcpdrill, an abortive close from a half-closed socket.
#
# c09 and c10 in tcp.drill assert the two abortive closes, unread data, and
# SO_LINGER with a zero timeout, from ESTABLISHED, and both pass.  Neither
# says anything about a socket that has already sent its FIN, which is where
# every program that does shutdown(SHUT_WR) and then decides to give up ends up.
#
# nx_tcp_socket_disconnect() refuses every state past CLOSE-WAIT, so from
# FIN-WAIT-1 or FIN-WAIT-2 the call that was meant to send the RESET returned
# NX_NOT_CONNECTED and sent nothing, and bsd_tcp_close_start() returned "the
# socket is finished with" either way.
#
# THE SEQUENCE NUMBER IS 2, NOT 1.  The FIN occupies one, so the RESET this side
# sends carries SND.NXT = ISN + 2.  That is the difference between these two
# cases and c09/c10, and the reason they are worth having: a RESET at 1 would be
# a sequence number the peer has already acknowledged.
#
# NEITHER CASE HAS EVER BEEN RUN.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

# SO_LINGER{1,0} after shutdown(SHUT_WR).  The FIN has gone and been
# acknowledged, so the socket is in FIN-WAIT-2; the close must still be a RESET.
case l01_linger_zero_after_shutdown_wr_resets
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
opt linger 0
shutdown wr
tx FA seq=1 ack=1
rx A seq=1 ack=2
close within=200
tx R seq=2

# RFC 1122 4.2.2.13, the same state reached the other way: the peer sent data
# after this side half-closed, nothing read it, and the close must not pretend
# it was delivered.
case l02_unread_data_after_shutdown_wr_resets
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
shutdown wr
tx FA seq=1 ack=1
rx A seq=1 ack=2
rx PA seq=1 ack=2 len=50
tx A seq=2 ack=51 within=400
close within=200
tx R seq=2

# The control, and the case that already passed: from ESTABLISHED the FIN has
# not gone, so the RESET carries 1.  Here so that a failure in l01 can be read
# as "the half-closed path" rather than "the abortive close".
case l03_linger_zero_from_established_still_resets
socket
connect
tx S seq=0
rx SA seq=0 ack=1 win=8192 mss=1460
tx A seq=1 ack=1
opt linger 0
close within=200
tx R seq=1
